# The dev container's build context is the repository's root, so that the image can install the
# toolchain from `mise.toml` and `mise.lock` (docs/decisions.md § D-29). Everything else in the
# checkout -- node_modules, .git, the worktrees under .claude/worktrees/ -- stays out of the context,
# which keeps the build fast and keeps the image from depending on anything the Dockerfile does not
# name. Docker reads this file, not a root .dockerignore, because its name is the Dockerfile's plus
# `.dockerignore`.
*
!mise.toml
!mise.lock
!.devcontainer/entrypoint.sh
